g) After the step of reading PLC_PC_Station2TorqueValue, the server goes to state 7. In state 7, the machine moves to Station 3, and this move is controlled by the PLC.
h) After the step of reading PLC_PC_Station3TorqueValue, the server goes to state 8. In state 8, the machine moves back to Station 2, and this move is controlled by the PLC.
i) At this stage, the machine is in Station 2, for a round of loosing and tightening of the nut again. We again read the torque value from PLC_PC_Station2TorqueValue. After this, the server goes to state 9
j) After another step of reading PLC_PC_Station3TorqueValue, the server goes to state 10. In state 10, the machine moves back to Station 2, and this move is controlled by the PLC.
k) After another step of reading PLC_PC_Station2TorqueValue, the server goes to state 11. In state 11, the machine moves to Station 3, and this move is controlled by the PLC.
l) After the step of reading PLC_PC_Station3TorqueValue, the server goes to state 12. In state 12, the machine moves back to Station 1, and this move is controlled by the PLC.
m) The server now waits for tag PLC_PC_CheckSplitPinAndWasher. After reading it, we do some activity and write back the result in tag PC_PLC_SplitPinAndWasherCheckingOK. The server goes to state 13
n) The server now waits for tag PLC_PC_CheckCap. After reading it, we do some activity and write back the result in tag PC_PLC_CapCheckingOK. The server goes to state 14
o) The server now waits for tag PLC_PC_CheckBung. After reading it, we do some activity and write back the result in tag PC_PLC_BungCheckingOK. The server goes to state 15
n) The server now waits for tag PLC_PC_CapPressDone. After reading it, the server goes to state 1, and waits for reading tag PLC_PC_CheckQRCode

